    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Feasible pilot\" sounds okay, but I'm worried that if we call it a \"pilot,\" the reviewers might dismiss the actual findings as being too preliminary for a major symposium. They'll look for high statistical power. Do you think we could instead frame the data collection as a highly controlled, high-fidelity way to capture these specific neuro-responses, making the small number actually an advantage for precision? I just want to make sure we don't give them an easy reason to reject the paper.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
